  "details": "Calling Camera.Render() on a camera in LateUpdate() or PostLateUpdate() will either crop the sides of or completely erase the contents of the current quick menu tab. \n\nWhen you open the menu the sides will be cropped.\n\nIf you switch to a different tab the contents there will display normally.\n\nIf you move to a different tab then close the menu and open it again, the menu will be completely empty. \n\nThe problem does not occur when called in Update().\n\nCamera component settings do not matter.\n\nThe problem only occurs in VR. \n\nThere are a few other reports about avatars breaking when rendering cameras in LateUpdate/PostLateUpdate that have gone unresolved for years, but no mention of the menu breaking. \n\nThe problem has been present for at least half a year.\n\nPC\n\nVRChat build: 1801\n\nSDK version: 3.10.2",
